KeePassPN
 * Feature: Brand icons for entries: the icon picker has a Brand tab with the logo of the brand that matches the web address of the entry; the logos are stored in the app, so nothing is downloaded, and choosing one saves it as a custom icon of the database
 * Change: text styles and buttons of the import, settings dialogs, about, entry and icon screens now use the Material 3 components
 * Security: the AES key derivation loop no longer cuts the number of rounds to 32 bits, and the AES rounds and Argon2 parallelism are limited to the values the code supports
 * Security: turning on automatic submit in Magikeyboard asks for confirmation first, because the form is then sent without another tap
 * Feature: Import entries from a CSV, JSON or ZIP file (one JSON file inside), including Proton Pass exports, from the bottom of the database settings; every entry and group of the file is imported as it is, with TOTP codes as verification codes, other values as custom fields, dates as entry dates, and a count of characters removed because a database cannot store them
 * Feature: "Verify before editing" in App settings > User Verification controls verification for editing entries and folders (on by default)
 * Feature: Trusted browsers for autofill under Form filling; only trusted browsers can tell autofill the current website
 * Feature: Long-press an entry or folder for edit, move to folder and duplicate; entries can be reordered by hand when the group allows it
 * Feature: Verification codes (2FA) screen with import from Google Authenticator exports and otpauth:// QR codes
 * Feature: TOTP Summary folder at the top of the root group lists the entries that already have a one-time password, with their live codes; its name can be changed by long-press
 * Feature: scanned codes are saved only to the 2FA group, which sits second at the root, after TOTP Summary
 * Feature: About > Check for updates shows the installed version and opens the release page
 * Change: the free and libre build variants are merged into one; build with ./gradlew assembleDebug
 * Change: the PIN check shows a progress bar and locks the input while it runs
 * Security: passkeys are offered only to privileged callers (verified browsers and allow-listed apps)
 * Security: saving writes to a temporary file first, so an interrupted save cannot replace the database with a partial file
 * Rename: the application is KeePassPN, package io.github.hidefbi.keepasspn
 * Feature: PIN unlock management in Settings > Device unlock (change PIN with the old PIN, disable PIN)
 * Feature: PIN validity of 7, 14, 30, 60 days or never
 * Change: three wrong PINs delete the PIN; two further wrong master passwords delete the database from the app
 * Feature: "Verify before copying" controls copy verification; user verification uses the database PIN, then the device credential, then the first four characters of the master password
 * Security: PIN wrap format v2 (Argon2id 64 MiB / 3 / 1, AAD bound to database URI and header)
 * Fix: a stale original no longer overwrites offline edits kept in the private recovery copy
